Scalability 
   measure of systems ability to handle a growing about of work , in an easy and cost effective way by adding resources to the system
 three option to scale
   Vertical scaling    - adding resources or upgrading the existing resources on a single computer , to allow system, to handle higher traffic load
   Horizontal scaling  - adding more resources in a form of new instances running on different machines , allows syste to handle higher traffic
   Team organisation scalability

Availability =  The fraction of the time or probability that the service is operationally functional and accessible to the users
   uptime = Time that our system is operationally functional and accessible to the users
   downtime = Time that the system is unavailable to the user
   availability (in %) = uptime / entire time the system is running (uptime + downtime)   || Availability = MTBF / (MTBF + MTTR)
MTBF = Mean Time Between Failure  , represents the average time the system is operational
     = looks at the entire systems hardware component , each componet has its own operational shelf life
     = cloud and service providers typically provide these ratios upfront
MTTR = Mean Time to Recovery , time average it takes to detect and recover from failure
     = average downtime of the system

